als": {"margin": 6.01, "lean": -5.0, "environment": 8.7, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.31}, "rating_margin": 3.4, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.65, "baseline_margin": 4.83, "analyst_adjustment": -0.33, "key_factors": ["Davis combines incumbency with a fundraising edge and has drawn far more outside spending against Buckhout than she has attracted for herself, even in a district redrawn to favor Republicans", "Available polls, though sponsored by partisan firms on both sides, mostly show Davis ahead by mid-to-high single digits, and prediction markets price his win odds near 80 percent", "Expert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, with a consensus near tilt-D, reflecting the tension between the R+5 new map and Davis's demonstrated strength", "Heavy Republican investment, including millions in outside money and a late Trump visit, keeps the race genuinely competitive"], "rationale": "Davis holds the structural advantages in a hostile new map: he has out-raised Buckhout, outside groups have spent heavily against her while little has attacked him, and the polls that exist plus prediction markets all point to a modest Democratic lead. Raters cluster between tossup and lean Democratic, which supports a small but real Davis edge rather than a pure tossup.", "watch": "A fresh nonpartisan poll, the effect of Trump's late-campaign visit, or a surge in Republican outside spending could pull the race back toward a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Don Davis (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Don Davis, a Democratic incumbent, is seeking another term in a North Carolina district redrawn to lean Republican by about five points. Despite the less favorable map, he has out-raised Laurie Buckhout and benefited from roughly $2.8 million in outside spending against her, while Republican outside support for Buckhout has been far smaller. Recent polls, though conducted by partisan-sponsored firms on both sides, mostly show Davis ahead by mid-to-high single digits, with one Republican-sponsored survey showing a one-point race. Prediction markets price his chances near 80 percent.\n\nExpert raters are split, with several calling the race a tossup and others leaning Democratic, and Republicans have invested heavily here, including a Trump visit in late October and spending that has made this the nation's costliest House race. The evidence points to a modest Davis advantage, but the redrawn electorate and the volume of money in play leave room for movement.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6957, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6748, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6753, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6236, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6194, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6727, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6943, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6373, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6827, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.694, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6664, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6646, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5982, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.63, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6926, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7256, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7195, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7176, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7197, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.6603, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.6738, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.6606, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.6674, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-18",